<h2>What a contemporary interior costs</h2>
<p>The style itself does not set the price; material grade and scope do. As a guide for Bangalore in 2026, a full contemporary interior costs about ₹700–1,100 per sq ft of carpet area in standard grade and ₹1,100–1,700 in premium grade, including GST. The contemporary look tends to shift money from decoration into lighting, concealed storage and a few quality pieces. For itemised budgets, see the <a href="/cost/2-bhk-interior-cost/">2 BHK</a> and <a href="/cost/3-bhk-interior-cost/">3 BHK</a> cost guides.</p>

<h2>Checklist before you brief a designer</h2>
<ul class="ticks">
  <li>Main palette decided for walls, floors and ceilings</li>
  <li>Lighting plan done before the furniture layout is frozen</li>
  <li>One Indian craft element chosen for each main room</li>
  <li>All storage counted and designed to be concealed</li>
  <li>Paint samples checked on the wall in daylight and at night</li>
  <li>AC, electrical and curtain-track positions fixed before false ceilings and paint</li>
  <li>A single hardware and fitting finish chosen for the whole home</li>
  <li>10–15% of the budget kept for surprises</li>
</ul>
